{#
  The ONE password exception, and it carries no secret: it only permits
  password authentication for one user on the public endpoint. The password
  itself lives in /etc/shadow and is set out of band (HOST_VARS.md
  §"The password is out of band"); this role never reads or writes it.

  `Match all` closes the block, so nothing appended after the Include in
  sshd_config can silently become part of this Match.
#}
# Included at the END of sshd_config, after all global directives.
# Restrict password authentication to {{ ssh_hardening_password_user }} on the explicit public endpoint.
Match User {{ ssh_hardening_password_user }} LocalAddress {{ ssh_hardening_public_address }} LocalPort {{ ssh_hardening_port }}
    PasswordAuthentication yes
Match all
